<h2>3. Accessing the website, hosting and server logs</h2>
<p>Our website is technically provided through Hetzner Online GmbH, Industriestraße 25, 91710 Gunzenhausen, Germany. When you visit the website, connection data required to deliver it and operate it securely is processed. This may include, in particular, your IP address, the date and time of access, the requested page or file, the HTTP status code, the volume of data transferred, the referrer URL and information about your browser and operating system.</p>
<p>This data is processed to provide the website, ensure stability and IT security, analyse errors and detect and prevent technical attacks. The legal basis is Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. Our legitimate interests are the secure, functional and uninterrupted provision of our online services.</p>
<p>Server log data is retained only for as long as necessary for operation, troubleshooting and security. The specific retention period depends on the server configuration used by the controller. Where log data is needed in an individual case to investigate a security incident or pursue legal claims, it may be retained longer to the extent necessary for that purpose.</p>
<p>Hetzner acts as a processor for hosting in accordance with Article 28 GDPR.</p>

<h2>4. Domain management and redirects</h2>
<p>The domain russ-live.de is managed through STRATO; this involves the data required for registration and technical domain management. The domains russ-live.com and michaelrussgmbh.de redirect to russ-live.de. When a website is accessed or a redirect takes place, the infrastructure used processes technically necessary connection data and, where applicable, log data. The legal basis is Article 6(1)(f) GDPR (availability and secure operation of our online services).</p>

<h2>5. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
<p>We do not currently use analytics or marketing services on this website to track user behaviour. We do not use a consent management tool because our current technical configuration does not use cookies or comparable technologies that require consent.</p>
<p>If strictly necessary cookies or comparable technologies are used, their sole purpose is to provide a service expressly requested by the user or enable technically necessary website functions. The exception under Section 25(2) of the German Telecommunications Digital Services Data Protection Act (TDDDG) may apply in this respect. Where personal data is processed in doing so, the processing is based on Article 6(1)(f) GDPR or, where applicable, Article 6(1)(b) GDPR.</p>
<p>If further technologies or services requiring consent are introduced in future, the necessary consent will be obtained before their use, where required, and this privacy notice will be updated.</p>

<h2>6. Contact by email or telephone</h2>
<p>If you contact us by telephone or email, we process the data you provide, particularly your name, contact details, the content of your message and the time and course of the communication, to handle your enquiry and, where necessary, agree further steps with you. There is no contact form on the website.</p>
<p>For pre-contractual or contractual matters, the legal basis is Article 6(1)(b) GDPR; for other enquiries, it is Article 6(1)(f) GDPR (our legitimate interest in appropriate communication and handling enquiries). Where statutory retention obligations apply, processing is based on Article 6(1)(c) GDPR.</p>
<p>We retain the data for as long as necessary to handle the matter. Longer retention may be required by statutory retention obligations or for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims.</p>
<p>Our email communication uses email services from STRATO, among others. Microsoft 365 / Exchange Online is also used for certain business communication processes, particularly in human resources. The email and IT service providers involved process technically necessary communication data and metadata and, where applicable, message content as part of their respective services.</p>

<h2>7. Applications and job vacancies</h2>
<p>You can prepare an application email in the job vacancies section. Initially, your entries remain on your device; the data is not stored as an online application through our web server. We receive your application documents only when you send the prepared email yourself.</p>
<p>After receiving an application, we process, in particular, contact details, application documents, qualifications and other information you provide to conduct the recruitment process and decide whether to enter into an employment relationship. The legal basis is Article 6(1)(b) GDPR. Where necessary for the defence or establishment of legal claims, further processing may be based on Article 6(1)(f) GDPR; the requirements of Article 9 GDPR also apply to special categories of personal data.</p>
<p>Incoming applications are processed through Microsoft 365 / Exchange Online and managed in an Outlook folder accessible to authorised persons. If an application is unsuccessful, application data is generally deleted six months after completion of the recruitment process, unless overriding retention grounds apply. If an applicant is hired, the information required for this purpose is transferred to personnel administration. No solely automated individual decision-making, including profiling within the meaning of Article 22 GDPR, takes place.</p>
<p>Further information about data categories, recipients, transfers to third countries and your rights is available in our separate “<a href="/datenschutz/bewerber">Privacy information for job applicants</a>”, provided alongside the job advertisements in the “Jobs” section.</p>

<h2>8. External links</h2>
<p>Our online services may contain links to other websites, including company websites, event listings, social networks and external ticket portals. These are simple external links; no external content, iframes, tracking pixels or other scripts from these providers are embedded on our website.</p>
<p>Merely visiting our website generally does not establish a connection to the linked websites solely because of the link. You only move to the respective provider when you click a link; that provider may process personal data as part of your visit. Information about this is available in the respective provider’s privacy notice.</p>

<h2>9. Recipients, processors and transfers of data to third countries</h2>
<p>Within the company, only departments and persons who need personal data for the relevant purposes are given access. Technical service providers, particularly for hosting, domain management, email communication and IT operations, may also receive data as processors or in another legally permissible capacity under data protection law. Where a processor relationship exists, an agreement is concluded in accordance with Article 28 GDPR.</p>
<p>The use of Microsoft 365 / Exchange Online may also involve Microsoft affiliates and subprocessors. Depending on the service and specific configuration, transfers to countries outside the European Economic Area, particularly the USA, cannot be entirely ruled out. Such transfers take place only subject to the requirements of Articles 44 et seq. GDPR, for example on the basis of an applicable adequacy decision covering the specific recipient or appropriate safeguards such as EU standard contractual clauses. We provide further information about the applicable safeguards on request.</p>

<h2>10. Data security</h2>
<p>We take appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect personal data. Our website is transmitted using HTTPS / TLS encryption. Please note that risks cannot be entirely ruled out when communicating by unencrypted email, even with technical safeguards in place.</p>

<h2>11. Your rights</h2>
<p>Subject to the statutory requirements, you have the following rights in particular: access to information about the processing of your data (Article 15 GDPR), rectification of inaccurate data (Article 16 GDPR), erasure (Article 17 GDPR), restriction of processing (Article 18 GDPR) and data portability (Article 20 GDPR).</p>
<p>Where we process personal data on the basis of Article 6(1)(e) or (f) GDPR, you may object to the processing on grounds relating to your particular situation in accordance with Article 21(1) GDPR. You may object to processing for direct marketing purposes at any time in accordance with Article 21(2) GDPR. You may withdraw consent given at any time with effect for the future (Article 7(3) GDPR); this does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out on the basis of consent before its withdrawal.</p>
<p>To exercise your rights, you can contact the responsible company or the data protection officer using the contact details provided above.</p>

<h2>12. Right to lodge a complaint</h2>
<p>Under Article 77 GDPR, you have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority, particularly at your habitual residence, place of work or the place of the alleged infringement. The supervisory authority responsible for us is, in particular:</p>
<p>Der Landesbeauftragte für den Datenschutz und die Informationsfreiheit Baden-Württemberg<br>Heilbronner Straße 35, 70191 Stuttgart<br>Phone: +49 (0) 711 615541-0<br>Email: poststelle@lfdi.bwl.de<br>Website: www.baden-wuerttemberg.datenschutz.de</p>

